    "text": "The point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>)</mo></math> (where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></math>&nbsp;is the greatest integer function) lying inside the region bounded by the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then",
